{"title":"Complementary angles","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Diagram\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Diagram</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Definitions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Definitions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Bing/Google\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Bing/Google</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Merriam-Webster\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Merriam-Webster</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Properties_and_Examples\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Properties and Examples</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Property\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Property</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Examples\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Examples</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Related_Topics\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Related Topics</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Diagram\">Diagram</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complementary_angles&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Diagram\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a75509ef276eae8b460d9b8cba0d1f1ad6b1b2ba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import olympiad; size(150); pair D = (0, 10), C = (10, 5), B = (10, 0), A = (0, 0); draw(A--B); draw(C--A); draw(D--A); markscalefactor=0.1; draw(rightanglemark((0,10),(0,0),(10,0))); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, NE); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"248\" />\n<p>As long as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/5/cb55dc9c50a80e1d9eb23fe53e45f464c0ac755e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> is a right angle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f105551f628f107282e0cc6c89063f3c1faece9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAD$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> are complementary angles to each other.\n</p>\n</center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Definitions\">Definitions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complementary_angles&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Definitions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span id=\"Bing.2FGoogle\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Bing/Google\">Bing/Google</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complementary_angles&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Bing/Google\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Either of two angles whose sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7dfa8a2a90d521b2b03f5b82a1fb9f85dce88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Merriam-Webster\">Merriam-Webster</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complementary_angles&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Merriam-Webster\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Two angles that add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> degrees\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Properties_and_Examples\">Properties and Examples</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complementary_angles&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Properties and Examples\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Property\">Property</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complementary_angles&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Property\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1ac662f7ddbbce489953c8b7693848239564aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" /> is complementary to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/2918f7d23f9ee8c04baabad86100d68023ec03f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/1/9f18187316325eca7223ef7b55e1615c2f6d7274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A + \\angle B = 90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8f350839bdb76d44e16c6b09ef4ea672ad88a4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{degrees}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Examples\">Examples</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complementary_angles&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Examples\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1ac662f7ddbbce489953c8b7693848239564aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0657f5cd42256c0a39d45b265235e2a939625515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8f350839bdb76d44e16c6b09ef4ea672ad88a4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{degrees}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/2918f7d23f9ee8c04baabad86100d68023ec03f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/866b44935f69a5b800547127fe13210bb1e36fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8f350839bdb76d44e16c6b09ef4ea672ad88a4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{degrees}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />, angle A and angle B are complementary since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a85b132ca9022c58bd7645bf025789a0994ed19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29 + 61 = 90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1ac662f7ddbbce489953c8b7693848239564aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8f350839bdb76d44e16c6b09ef4ea672ad88a4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{degrees}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/2918f7d23f9ee8c04baabad86100d68023ec03f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/6/3e67376d85a21889a01b76d7c9d8c765b2bac379.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$62$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8f350839bdb76d44e16c6b09ef4ea672ad88a4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{degrees}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />, angle A and angle B are not complementary since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/e/2be21321a691aa235173afb5c86d3fd4bb5f99a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 + 62 = 92$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" />, and not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8f350839bdb76d44e16c6b09ef4ea672ad88a4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{degrees}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Related_Topics\">Related Topics</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complementary_angles&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Related Topics\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complementary\" title=\"Complementary\">Complementary</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle\" title=\"Angle\">Angle</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Complementary_angles&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017235339\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.035 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 159/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 301/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4868/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.725      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.725      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17967:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017235339 and revision id 194017. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}